PICTURES (user, Oct 16 2026; more Oct 17, from the user's comments)

  Every AVS mesh file a test writes (*.inp that is not one of its
  inputs) is drawn: logs/pics/<test>__NN.svg, shown on the test's row
  (click one to open it full size). A test that writes no mesh file
  (filter, quality, surface, grid2grid, ... about 15 of them) is run a
  SECOND time in work/_pic_<test>, with one line added before its
  first finish: "dump / avs / zz_final_mesh.inp" (the current mesh
  object), and that end state is drawn. The judged run is always the
  test's own deck, unchanged. Files of more than 250 000 cells or
  400 000 vertices are not drawn (createpts_filter's end state has a
  million vertices). Point and cell sets, .stor and zone files are not
  meshes and are not drawn.
  OCTREE meshes (refine / amr keeps every level: a refined hex stays in
  the mesh with its 8 children): only the LEAVES are drawn (user, Oct
  16). With the cell attribute itetkid in the file (dump / avs / f /
  mo / 1 1 1 1) a cell with itetkid > 0 is a parent; without it, a hex
  is a parent when a hex that shares one of its vertices is less than
  half its size and has its centre inside it. Checked on refine_octree:
  both ways give the same 1034 parents of 8322 cells, and the 7288
  leaves fill the box exactly (volume 0.05; all levels together 0.119).
  The picture says how many parent cells were left out. Same camera as test_createpts
  (right-handed: x cross y shows as z), axis icon bottom left.

COMMENTING ON THE PAGE (user, Oct 16 2026)

  Every test has a comment box (as on the test_createpts page): type
  what to implement or change for that test; an empty box means no
  change. Comments stay in this browser (per suite) until "Clear all".
  "Copy all comments" puts them on the clipboard; "Save as file" writes
  test_lagrit_upstream_comments.txt to Downloads: attach it in the chat.
  Each comment is listed with its test and that test's result.

  Oct 17 (user's comments): the interpolate tests (interp_continuous,
  interp_map, interp_voronoi) show one pair per interpolate command,
  the command above it: the SOURCE coloured by the source attribute,
  the SINK after the command coloured by the sink attribute, on one
  colour scale; when the sink is a horizontal plane, the source is
  seen from above too, at the same scale and position, so the two
  patterns line up. pset: vertices by imt; smooth_massage: aspect
  ratio; quad_quality: quality, qflag, regularity; quality: the six
  single test tets on one aspect-ratio scale. All set in pictures.txt.

EXPLANATIONS

  notes.txt holds a short explanation per test (what it does, what the
  pictures show, what each measure means); it is shown on the test's
  row. Written for: interp_continuous, interp_map, interp_voronoi,
  quality, quad_quality, pset, pset_readwrite, pflotran_stor,
  smooth_massage, io_agf_simple (the NaN question), recon1,
  refine_octree, refine_octree_prd.

READING THE PAGE

  A link at the top goes back to the top-level summary (all suites).
  The top lists every test that does not PASS, with a link to its row.
  Each row: a comment box, the pictures, the note, then fold-outs:
  "output files against the truth" (opened when one differs), "our
  own check", "LaGriT's diff" (when the log differs) and "LaGriT
  control file".
  Each row: result, time, and fold-outs: "LaGriT's diff" (the lines
  that differ, reference line first, "-" reference, "+" output) and
  "LaGriT control file" (the test's input.lgi).

ADDING A TEST

  Add it to LaGriT's own test/level01 (a folder with input.lgi and
  reference/outx3dgen made by a trusted build); this suite picks it up.
  Tests of our own go in our other suites.
